Router2 sends v1 broadcasts → router1 ignores them. Router1 sends v2 multicast → router2 ignores them. Routes on both sides time out at 180s, get marked metric-16 (infinity), and are being garbage-collected. This explains exactly why reachability from the Phase 1 snapshot showed 0% loss (routes were still alive at age 174s) but the user observed recurring disappearances.

